      "finding": null,
      "explanation": "There is a significant scope mismatch between the declared purpose and actual implementation. The description claims the skill handles 8+ distinct PDF operations (merging, splitting, rotating, watermarking, encryption, OCR, etc.), but the actual codebase implements only form-field-specific operations. Specifically:\n\n**Capabilities NOT implemented but DECLARED:**\n- Merging/combining PDFs\n- Splitting PDFs into separate files\n- Rotating PDF pages\n- Adding watermarks to PDFs\n- Encrypting/decrypting PDFs\n- Extracting text or tables from PDFs\n- Extracting images from PDFs\n- OCR on scanned PDFs to make them searchable\n- Creating new/blank PDFs\n\n**Capabilities ACTUALLY implemented but NOT described:**\n- Extracting and analyzing form field information from fillable PDFs (detailed field type detection, page locations, radio buttons, checkboxes, choice fields)\n- Extracting structural information from non-fillable PDFs (text labels with coordinates, horizontal lines, checkbox detection)\n- Validating form field bounding boxes for intersections and sizing issues\n- Converting PDF pages to PNG images with scaling\n- Filling fillable PDF forms with field values and validation\n- Filling non-fillable PDFs with text annotations at specified coordinates\n\nThe actual skill is narrowly focused on PDF form processing workflows (extraction \u2192 validation \u2192 filling), not general-purpose PDF manipulation. This represents a material difference in primary purpose and scope.",
